  "notes": "The process of cutting logs into usable boards, planks, and lumber.\n\nFORMS:\n{製|せい} (manufacture, process) + {材|ざい} (material, timber)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {製材|せいざい}{所|じょ}: sawmill\n- {製材|せいざい}{業|ぎょう}: lumber industry\n- {製材|せいざい}{品|ひん}: sawn lumber products\n- {丸太|まるた}を{製材|せいざい}する: to saw a log into lumber\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {木材|もくざい}: timber, lumber (the finished product)\n- {丸太|まるた}: log (raw, unprocessed)\n- {合板|ごうはん}: plywood\n- {林業|りんぎょう}: forestry industry\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nJapan has a significant domestic timber industry. Famous production regions include {吉野|よしの} (Nara), {秋田|あきた}, and {北海道|ほっかいどう}.",
